<title>UK: TransCo UK gas forecasts for February 12.</title>
<headline>TransCo UK gas forecasts for February 12.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>TransCo, the pipeline division of British Gas plc, has announced the following forecasts and data for gas use in the period February 10-12.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>Feb 10 (actual) 311 million cubic metres, 73 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Feb 11 (forecast) 315 million cubic metres, 74 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Feb 12 (forecast) 303 million cubic metres, 71 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>Feb 10 (actual) 6.4 Celsius, seasonal normal 4.1 Celsius</p>
<p>Feb 11 (forecast) 8.8 Celsius, seasonal normal 4.2 Celsius</p>
<p>Feb 12 (forecast) 8.6 Celsius, seasonal normal 4.2 Celsius</p>
<p>There were no interruptions in any of the 13 Local Distribution Zones on Tuesday, and the probability of interruption in all areas on Wednesday is &quot;low&quot;.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
